  "id": "pokemon-center-new-york-opening",
  "name": "Pokémon Center New York opening",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Nintendo opened the Pokémon Center in New York at Rockefeller Center on 16 November 2001, and gave out two cards drawn by \"Big Mama\" Tagawa at its opening, Wizards Black Star Promos 40 Pokémon Center and 41 Lucky Stadium. In January 2002 the Pokémon Centers in Tokyo and Osaka marked the opening with cards of their own, Pokémon Center Tokyo 019/P, showing Pikachu in the store, and Pokémon Center Osaka 020/P, showing Meowth by its sign. The New York store closed in 2005, when the Nintendo World Store replaced it.",
